= Solution
{parent=a}

For every integer $t$,
$$
P(\mathbb P_k^2,\mathcal O,t)=\chi(\mathbb P_k^2,\mathcal O(t))
=\binom{t+2}{2}
=\frac{t^2+3t+2}{2}.
$$
For $t\geq0$ this is the dimension of the homogeneous polynomials of degree $t$, since the higher cohomology vanishes; polynomiality then identifies the <Hilbert polynomial>.

= b
{parent=ii}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

A smooth plane curve of degree $m$ has genus
$$
g=\frac{(m-1)(m-2)}2.
$$
The line bundle $\mathcal O_X(D)(t)$ has degree $d+mt$. The <Riemann-Roch theorem> therefore gives
$$
P(X,\mathcal O_X(D),t)
=\chi(\mathcal O_X(D)(t))
=mt+d+1-g
=mt+d+1-\frac{(m-1)(m-2)}2.
$$

